rability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.03548460276536317,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.19297332006847445,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0034400001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"AGNC Investment Corp. provides private capital to housing market in the United States. It invests in residential mortgage pass-through securities and collateralized mortgage obligations for which the principal and interest payments are guaranteed by the United States government-sponsored enterprise or by the United States government agency. The company qualifies as a real estate investment trust for federal income tax purposes. It generally would not be subject to federal or state corporate income taxes if it distributes at least 90% of its taxable income to its stockholders. The company was formerly known as American Capital Agency Corp. and changed its name to AGNC Investment Corp. in September 2016. AGNC Investment Corp. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Bethesda, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter J. Federico | President, CEO & Director and Chief Investment Officer | Age 59 | Compensation: $8.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 54 people. Stock-based compensation of $481K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["AGNC Investment Corp. is a large-cap real estate business with a $10.5B market cap.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 3.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 45% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","17 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Where Will AGNC Investment Stock Be in 5 Years?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/where-agnc-investment-stock-5-195000000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794600104.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AGNC Investment Corp. Declares Monthly Common Stock Dividend of $0.12 per Common Share for November 2026","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/agnc-investment-corp-declares-monthly-common-stock-dividend-of-0-12-per-common-share-for-november-2026--302938156.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794517260.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"AGNC Investment (AGNC) Stock Looks Overpriced Against Its Sales Base","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-agnc/agnc-investment/news/agnc-investment-agnc-stock-looks-overpriced-against-its-sale","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794443721.411,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.931,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"4 REIT Dividend Traps Where Payouts Could Be in Danger","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/12/4-reit-dividend-traps-where-payouts-could-be-in-danger/","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794493956.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"A $900,000 Portfolio That Quietly Pays $60,000 a Year Without Touching Principal","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/art